<title>USA: Strober bidder withdraws $6.50/shr offer.</title>
<headline>Strober bidder withdraws $6.50/shr offer.</headline>
<dateline>BROOKLYN, N.Y. 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Strober Organization Inc said on Tuesday an undisclosed third party bidder did not wish to pursue its acquisition of the company and had withdrawn its $6.50 per share offer.</p>
<p>On November 11, Strober said it entered a definitive merger deal with a private venture capital investor group which planned to buy outstanding Strober stock for $6 per share. On December 5, Strober said it received a third unsolicited $6.50 per share bid for the company.</p>
<p>Strober said the original bid from November 11 was still in place and parties contemplated completing the transaction in February 1997.</p>
<p>((-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
